+### REQ-REPORT-5850: V521 Post-Marker Source Delta Ingestion Preserves Sealed Planner Boundaries
+
+The Exp5850 workflow SHALL run a bounded execution refresh after the
+`V521-PLANNER-REFRESH-20260723-END` marker and SHALL write
+`results/experiment_5850_v521_source_delta_ingestion.json`. It SHALL first hash
+the V521 planner marker block, active roadmap task IDs and gate content,
+optional `research-roadmap-next.yaml` task IDs and gate content when present,
+`research-references.md`, `ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml`, and active
+`research-roadmap.yaml`. It SHALL record network and source availability for
+all requested routes, and SHALL record unavailable or rate-limited routes as
+explicit outcomes rather than inferred source claims. If the marker is absent,
+no primary or secondary route is reachable, or roadmap immutability cannot be
+checked, the workflow SHALL emit a terminal `blocked:` artifact and SHALL leave
+`research-references.md`, `research-roadmap.yaml`, optional
+`research-roadmap-next.yaml`, and `scripts/research_conductor.py` unchanged.
+
+The workflow SHALL search arXiv first for newer EBM verification/reasoning,
+neural CSPs, Ising/sampling, hallucination verification, KANs,
+energy-guided decoding, probabilistic hardware, continual learning, and active
+observation. It SHALL then check OpenReview, Hugging Face Papers, direct
+Semantic Scholar citation routes for EBT `2507.02092` and ARM-EBM
+`2512.15605`, GitHub discovery, Extropic writing/hardware, and Logical
+Intelligence public pages. Every surfaced item SHALL be classified as
+`accepted`, `duplicate`, `watch_only`, `inaccessible`, or `excluded` with URL,
+date, query or receipt id, access outcome, and reason.
+
+The workflow MAY complete with zero accepted findings. Accepted findings SHALL
+be newer than the V521 planner marker or newly actionable only after that
+sealed marker, non-duplicate, and mapped to bounded controls inside allocated
+Exp5851-Exp5861 scopes. Accepted findings SHALL NOT rewrite task identities,
+structured gates, mandatory SOTA models, retired scopes, hardware claims,
+headline authority, or active roadmap task identity. The workflow SHALL NOT
+reopen generated-answer transport, PHASE D output-text/logit work, tempering,
+public ARC solves, cross-game value transfer, unchanged board probes, TSU
+execution, or Kona execution. When no accepted non-duplicate finding exists,
+the workflow SHALL leave `research-references.md` unchanged and set
+`accepted_finding_count=0` and `references_modified=false`. When an accepted
+finding exists, it MAY append exactly one dated execution-refresh block without
+rewriting the V521 planner block.
+
+The artifact SHALL include, at minimum, `status`, `preconditions_checked`,
+`planner_marker_and_search_window`, `source_receipts`,
+`citation_trail_receipts`, `finding_classification`,
+`accepted_finding_count`, `references_modified`,
+`roadmap_immutability_receipts`, `duration_s`, `inference_substrate`,
+`field_provenance`, `test_commands`, `test_exit_codes`,
+`reproducibility_checksum`, and `honest_verdict`. It SHALL set
+`inference_substrate="aggregation_from_external_primary_sources"`. Every
+required top-level field SHALL have a non-empty field-provenance principle. The
+`honest_verdict` SHALL start with `complete:` or `blocked:` so a complete zero
+delta cannot be confused with a failed search.
+
+Required field principles:
+
+- `status`: principle "A terminal state distinguishes a complete zero delta from failed research."
+- `preconditions_checked`: principle "Marker, hash, and network checks prevent stale-window or fabricated-source claims."
+- `planner_marker_and_search_window`: principle "A sealed time boundary makes novelty falsifiable."
+- `source_receipts`: principle "Queries, URLs, dates, and outcomes separate primary evidence from discovery metadata."
+- `citation_trail_receipts`: principle "Direct EBT and ARM-EBM checks prevent unsupported citation claims."
+- `finding_classification`: principle "Explicit classes stop duplicates and watch items becoming experiments."
+- `accepted_finding_count`: principle "A bare zero is a valid complete result."
+- `references_modified`: principle "The artifact discloses whether the shared source ledger changed."
+- `roadmap_immutability_receipts`: principle "Freshness work cannot silently redesign allocated tasks."
+- `duration_s`: principle "Measured time exposes a bootstrap-only receipt."
+- `inference_substrate`: principle "`aggregation_from_external_primary_sources` declares literature synthesis, not experiment inference."
+- `field_provenance`: principle "Every accepted finding maps to its source and existing task hook."
+- `test_commands`: principle "Commands document date, duplicate, citation, and immutability checks."
+- `test_exit_codes`: principle "Exit codes prevent failed provenance checks becoming success."
+- `reproducibility_checksum`: principle "A checksum detects marker, reference, or classification drift."
+- `honest_verdict`: principle "A `complete:` or `blocked:` prefix makes the refresh terminal."
+
+#### SCENARIO-REPORT-5850-ZERO-FINDING: Complete Zero Delta Leaves References Unchanged
+
+**Given** the V521 planner marker is present, arXiv and at least one secondary
+source family are reachable, and every surfaced item is duplicate, watch-only,
+excluded, or inaccessible
+**When** the Exp5850 workflow runs
+**Then** it writes `results/experiment_5850_v521_source_delta_ingestion.json`,
+sets `status=complete`, records every required source family and citation
+route, sets `accepted_finding_count=0`, keeps `references_modified=false`,
+preserves roadmap IDs and gates, preserves closed scopes and hardware/headline
+claims, and emits a `complete:` verdict.
+
+#### SCENARIO-REPORT-5850-ACCEPT-BOUNDED-DELTA: Accepted Findings Stay Inside Exp5851-Exp5861
+
+**Given** a source is post-marker or newly actionable after the V521 marker,
+non-duplicate, and only adds a bounded control inside Exp5851-Exp5861
+**When** the source is accepted
+**Then** the artifact and optional reference append record source id, title,
+URL, date, receipt, target experiment, source hook, authority-boundary reason,
+and field provenance while preserving roadmap IDs, structured gates, mandatory
+SOTA models, retired scopes, hardware claims, and headline authority.
+
+#### SCENARIO-REPORT-5850-BLOCKED-PRECONDITION: Missing Marker Or Source Reachability Blocks
+
+**Given** the V521 marker is absent or no primary or secondary source route is
+reachable
+**When** the Exp5850 workflow runs
+**Then** it writes a terminal blocked artifact, records the failed
+precondition, keeps `accepted_finding_count=0`, keeps
+`references_modified=false`, leaves references unchanged, and starts
+`honest_verdict` with `blocked:`.
+
+#### SCENARIO-REPORT-5850-CLOSED-SCOPE-IMMUTABILITY: Roadmap And Retired Scopes Are Protected
+
+**Given** a candidate would reopen generated-answer transport, PHASE D
+output-text/logit work, tempering, public ARC solves, cross-game value
+transfer, unchanged board probes, TSU execution, Kona execution, or rewrite
+task IDs, gates, mandatory SOTA models, hardware claims, or headline authority
+**When** the candidate is classified
+**Then** it is excluded or watch-only, closed scopes remain closed, roadmap
+immutability receipts stay unchanged, and no hardware or headline claim is
+altered.
+
+#### SCENARIO-REPORT-5850-SCHEMA: Required Fields And Provenance Are Stable
+
+**Given** the Exp5850 artifact is emitted
+**When** the artifact schema is validated
+**Then** every required top-level field has field provenance, every source
+receipt has query, URL, date, and access outcome metadata, every candidate
+classification is in the allowed set, direct EBT and ARM-EBM citation receipts
+are present, and the checksum is stable.
+
